OCPARTICLE 2
NAME Beam Ribbon
# Wave 10 demo: a linked ribbon -- consecutive particles are joined into ONE continuous strip (a beam, a whip, a banner of light).
# 64 particles are emitted a second with a one second life, so the strip is always 64 links long, and curl noise makes it
# writhe. Emitting along +X from the emitter: place the instance and watch the strip stream out of it.
PARAM Wriggle float 25
EMITTER Beam
SIM auto
SHAPE point 0 0 0
BLEND additive
EMISSION 64 0 64
LIFETIME 1 1
DIRECTION 1 0 0 0
SPEED 300 300
GRAVITY 0 0 0
DAMPING 0
SIZE 14 2
COLORCURVE 0 0.4 0.8 1 0 0.2 0.5 0.9 1 1 1 0.15 0.3 0.8 0
RENDER ribbon linked 64
SORT none
LIGHTING unlit
FOG on
BOUNDS 600
MODULE update.curlnoise freq=0.015 strength=@Wriggle scroll=1 octaves=2 seed=21
